LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP/Navigation/","source-block-937","different from go to definition (lowercase d) because declaration is the implementation, the current context, just like how many of the LazyVim keyshorts use shift to be the modifier for \"current directory\" rather than \"repository.\" The declaration, that is, the implementation, is \"local,\" while the definition or interface is \"global.\"",["Keyshort LazyVim LazyVim/Keyshort LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP","Go to Declaration Card","Mnemonic"]],["LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP/Navigation/","source-block-1282","Go to Implementation Card",["Keyshort LazyVim LazyVim/Keyshort LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP"]],["LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP/Navigation/","source-block-1515","Shortcut: gI",["Keyshort LazyVim LazyVim/Keyshort LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP","Go to Implementation Card"]],["LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP/Navigation/","source-block-1534","Description: Jumps to the symbol's implementation.",["Keyshort LazyVim LazyVim/Keyshort LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP","Go to Implementation Card"]],["LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP/Navigation/","source-block-1589","Go to References Card",["Keyshort LazyVim LazyVim/Keyshort LazyVim/Keyshort/LSP"]]],"format_version":5}